Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a rounding along a chain whose faces turn into their neighbours at
creases of a few degrees, both faces at nearly the same section (mitcad#343).

The case: a fin's top edges rounded with 0.2, the fin's top an arc and a
straight part, its sides chamfered along the arcs only; slivers join the
chamfers to the straight part's sides, and every face meets the next at a
crease of one to five degrees, which OCCT's fillet takes for tangent
(normals within a tenth of a radian). The selected edges are the arcs' and
the straight parts' edges; between them short edges of the slivers, the
chain kinked by about a degree and a half there.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformElement, StopChainsAtTurns: a contour does not
  stop at a turn before an edge not asked for that leads, its faces going
  on tangentially at its other vertex, to an edge asked for (a short edge
  between two edges of one tangent chain). Before, each selected edge was
  its own contour, ending at a vertex of four sharp edges, where the
  corner failed.
- ChFi3d_PerformElSpine: the guide of a walk that starts a hair (less
  than a hundredth of its length) short of the end of its edge after an
  analytic piece of the stripe (or ends a hair past the start of one) is
  built from a stretch of that edge before (after) it as well, its own
  parameters kept: its first span was that hair, the kink of the spine at
  the edge's end turned within it, and the guide extrapolated past its
  start left the spine at once. The first section's reframing, which
  looks a little before the start, found no section on its arcs, and the
  walk failed.
- ChFi3d_Builder::ComputeData, KinkIntoEndFace: a face crossed onto at a
  kink that holds the spine's end vertex is the face at the end only when
  no edge of the spine lies on it; before, the walk onto the fin's top,
  whose straight part runs to the end vertex, stopped there.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: where the piece before ended
  with one contact crossing onto a face continuing its own tangentially
  and the other within ten times the approximation tolerance of an edge
  of its face, ahead, across which its face goes on tangentially too,
  that contact changes face as well; BRepBlend_Walking::PerformFirstSection
  starts such a section on both arcs where the two reach them within ten
  times the guide's tolerance of each other (at the later section, its
  other contact a hair past its arc). Before, a walk on one new face and
  one old was taken between, out of order with its neighbours, and their
  contact lines overlapped on the slivers.
- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol: a face taken for tangent that meets the face
  before at a concave crease of more than the angular tolerance does not
  continue it: the ball turns about the crease's edge (a walk rolling on
  it, from the ball of the piece before) until it touches that face, its
  reference face, and leaves the edge onto it. The edge is taken on the
  face whose part beside the piece of the crease stays (the face before
  where the crease runs away from the spine, else the face beyond).
  ComputeData does not complete such a walk back forward over the piece
  before (ChFi3d_SetStartsAtPieceBefore), and ChFi3d_FilDS gives the
  crease's point where a piece leaves it onto the face it rolled on as
  that face's only the transition of the piece leaving (with both, the
  edge was cut twice there). Before, the walk on the next face started
  some 0.1 mm further on than the one before ended, the gap closed by
  edge tolerances of 0.1 mm.

On the design's body before the item (its 12 edges, chains kept at turns
as the import asks): valid, every face on the stored body's within 0.0083
mm and every face of the stored body on the result's within 0.0024 mm, the
change of volume -0.2909 against the file's -0.2888 mm3; before, OCCT's
corners at the four-edge vertices failed. Synthetic: a box's top front
edges rounded with 1 and 0.5 where the front turns outward by 3 and 5
degrees about a slanted crease from the top edge, the edges given either
way: valid, no edge tolerance above 1e-4, the material taken within 0.5 %
of the two edges' sections along them; before, the fillet failed at a
vertex.

Upstream: new.

